.claude
.git
.github
node_modules
tasks
.worktrees
# The agent-skills staging clone (build.sh populates it) holds a whole repo —
# its own .git, docs, and non-Codex flavor dirs — but the Dockerfile COPYs only
# the subpaths re-included below: .agent-skills-src/codex/dev-skills/skills/
# (the Codex skill palette) plus the single-source-of-truth helpers baked to
# /usr/local/bin from .agent-skills-src/plugins/dev-skills/bin/ (gh-review-threads,
# and the disposable-clone pair dc-enter/dc-remove). Exclude the entire staging
# tree and re-include just those, so the rest (notably .git) never enters the
# build context: smaller context uploads and no unrelated files exposed to a
# remote builder. Keep this list in step with the Dockerfile's COPY — a helper
# baked without its re-include here fails the build on a missing COPY source.
# Nested re-include under an excluded parent is honored by both BuildKit and
# buildah/podman.
.agent-skills-src
!.agent-skills-src/codex/dev-skills/skills
!.agent-skills-src/plugins/dev-skills/bin/gh-review-threads
!.agent-skills-src/plugins/dev-skills/bin/dc-enter
!.agent-skills-src/plugins/dev-skills/bin/dc-remove
